      "component_id": "ED26-P15-CH-independent-random-variables-C001",
      "verdict": "partial",
      "gap": "The held source defines independence of an arbitrary infinite collection of sigma-fields, random variables or sets as independence of every finite subcollection (Durrett 2019, sec. 2.1, p. 44), with no cardinality restriction; the source's uncorrelated-family definition at p. 56 likewise uses an arbitrary index family i in I. The handbook entry restricts the index set to a finite or countably infinite I (IP 28-29) and never defines independence for an uncountable family, without identifying this restriction as a departure from the source. A narrower regime is substituted for the source definition, so the identified source variant is not preserved.",
